# Where are you going in Russian: куда?
subtitle: "Ask and say where you're going in Russian with идти́ and куда́, and see how a place changes on the way: в Москве́ when you're there, в Москву́ when you go."
teaches: ["grammar/verbs-of-motion","grammar/object-ending"]
thumb: "band \"Where to? Not where.\" note \"где? → куда́?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"I have in Russian: у меня есть","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/28-russian-have.cast"}

## Where are you going in Russian: куда?
level: basic

